Based on Clause 5.5.4.3 (UE-initiated authentication and key agreement procedure initiation), upon receiving a ProSe direct link establishment request from the 5G ProSe remote UE including the SUCI of the 5G ProSe remote UE, for establishing a secure PC5 unicast link as specified in 3GPP TS 24.554, when the security for 5G ProSe communication via 5G ProSe UE-to-network relay is performed over control plane as specified in 3GPP TS 33.503, the UE (acting as the 5G ProSe UE-to-network relay) shall perform the following specific actions:

a) **Allocate a PRTI value** – as specified in clause 5.5.4.2, the UE shall allocate an available ProSe Relay Transaction Identity (PRTI) value and associate it with the 5G ProSe remote UE;

b) **Create a RELAY KEY REQUEST message**;

c) **Set the PRTI IE** of the RELAY KEY REQUEST message to the allocated PRTI value;

d) **Set the relay key request parameters IE** of the RELAY KEY REQUEST message using the SUCI, relay service code, and nonce_1 received from the 5G ProSe remote UE;

e) **Send the RELAY KEY REQUEST message** (toward the network, e.g., AMF); and

f) **Start timer T35xx** upon sending the RELAY KEY REQUEST message.

Additionally, per clause 5.5.4.2, the allocated PRTI value shall be released when the authentication and key agreement procedure for 5G ProSe UE-to-network relay completes or is aborted.

This sequence initiates the authentication and key agreement procedure for the 5G ProSe UE-to-network relay (per clause 5.5.4.1), whereby the network subsequently decides whether to process the relay key request and, if so, controls an EAP-based authentication and key agreement procedure whose EAP messages are relayed between the 5G ProSe remote UE and the network by this UE (acting as relay).

When Identity type IE = "SUCI" and T3519 is **not running**, the UE shall:

1. Generate a **fresh SUCI**, as specified in 3GPP TS 33.501 [24];
2. Send an **IDENTITY RESPONSE** message containing this newly generated SUCI;
3. **Start timer T3519**; and
4. **Store the value of the SUCI** that was sent in the IDENTITY RESPONSE message.

This ensures that, while T3519 remains running, any subsequent IDENTITY REQUEST for a SUCI will use the stored (already generated) SUCI rather than generating a new one, per clause 5.4.3.3.
